From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Faust <willtechnoduck@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 14:06:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iOS: dual-map fast-write infra (trap-mode default) + iOS 27
 hardening

- Buffer.h/DualMap.h/JIT.cpp/Dispatcher.cpp: FEX_IOS_HOST dual-map
  WritePtr machinery + inline dc/ic flush helpers. Runtime-disabled:
  ProcessInit forces WriteOffset=0 (trap-mode - writes fault to Wine's
  Mach emulator, which also handles icache). The direct-write path
  corrupted x86->EC transitions (msvcp140 DllMain EH, Goldberg
  steam_api64 init) and needs a rework (NtFlushInstructionCache)
  before enabling. Bisect-verified: trap-mode reaches the 3D menu on
  iOS 27; fast-write dies pre-splash.
- Module.cpp: read pool geometry from WINE_IOS_JIT_RW/RX env (RW alias
  is not guaranteed at RX+0x10000000 on iOS 27); IOSLoadTEB()
  (TPIDRRO_EL0/TSD-275) replaces raw-x18 NtCurrentTeb in GetCPUArea +
  LoadStateFromECContext (iOS 27 clobbers x18 aggressively).
- Dispatcher.cpp: dispatcher entry derives STATE via the TPIDRRO chain
  instead of trusting caller x0 (exit-linker reached entry with x0=0;
  page-0 Mach emulation masked the null state until the
  ReturningStackLocation store at +0x5c0 faulted).
- Core.cpp: silence per-block IR logging (perf).

